  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "To work around the raycast not being accessible from the Interact event, I made my own via the InputUse event. My issue now is that this isn't supported via the current Alpha mobile touchscreen interface. Not only can I not grab the interaction raycast, but now I also cannot grab an InputUse event since, via the mobile touchscreen, it requires an interactive object for the UI for it to display.\n\nMy main example for why this is useful is I have terrain that is essentially interactive. Ideally I don't want the entire world to light up as an interactable object too and would like to conditionally display InteractionText.\n\nI would love to request that there is a way to attempt an InputUse event regardless if there's an interactable on screen.\n\nOR (\n\nThe raycast used (or a duplicate when an Interact event is defined with a Raycast argument) when determining there's an Interactable object exists to Use is exposed via Interact(Raycast cast)\n\nAND\n\nThat HideInteract is implemented alongside the existing DisableInteract to hide the Interact highlight while still allowing the Interact event to be called and optionally allowing the InteractionText to still be visible via a bool argument.\n\n)\n\nTo explain the current systems in the screenshots, I'm using the InputUse event to spawn a raycast. Where the raycast origin is depends on if VRControllers are being used. In the case of mobile, there's not parity with PC Desktop mode being able to press Use at any time. Also attempting to emulate a raycast from where the player uses their touch screen, rather than the origin of their current view, doesn't seem currently feasible.",
